request.description:
Single delivery detail ("Next Delivery" card / "Full Delivery Instructions" dialog). Same shape as a Get Deliveries list item, including:
  loadAndBundle{loadId, bundleCount, truckNumber, totalWeight}
  packingListSummary{totalParts, bundleTypes, material}
  receivingPoc / siteContact {name, phone, email} (same underlying contact — the model only has one real site-contact field)
  deliveryTeam / deliveryCompany {company/name, driver, phone, email}

Run 'Get Upcoming Deliveries' first to populate {{deliveryId}}.

"Send SMS" button in the Contact Driver dialog. message is optional — a sensible default is used if omitted.

NOTE: No SMS provider (Twilio) is configured yet. This returns success and logs the message server-side (provider: 'stub') so the dialog works end-to-end; real delivery will start once Twilio credentials are added.

Returns: { message, sms }

Powers the "Contact Delivery Company" dialog.

Returns: { delivery{title,deliveryNumber,status}, managerName, managerPhone, companyName }

Returns 404 if no carrier has been selected yet.

Powers the "Add to Calendar" dialog's content (event card, Google/Outlook deep links, copy-to-clipboard text). This is JSON, not a file download — use 'Add to Calendar (.ics)' below for the actual downloadable file.

Returns: { title, description, location, startDate, endDate, googleCalendarUrl, outlookCalendarUrl, icsDownloadUrl, plainText }

Returns 400 if the delivery has no deliveryDate set yet.

